# Spaghetti Checker — One Context Per File

Keep each file focused on a single responsibility. Too much in one file hurts
readability, reviewability, and testability.

**Enforcement:** `npm run check:spaghetti` (also in Husky pre-commit and Cursor
`afterFileEdit` / `stop` hooks). Fix all violations before declaring work done.

---

## Canonical module layout `src/modules/<name>/`

```
<name>/
  pages/                 # route-level page components
  components/            # one React component per .tsx
  hooks/                 # one hook per file
  schemas/               # Zod form validation
  services/              # business logic
  stores/                # Zustand slice (if needed)
  types/
  routes.ts              # re-exports pages only — no component bodies
  __tests__/             # Vitest + Testing Library tests
```

| File               | Allowed contents                              |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |
| `routes.ts`        | `export { XPage } from './pages/x-page'` only |
| `pages/*.tsx`      | Single page component                         |
| `components/*.tsx` | Single component                              |
| `hooks/*.ts`       | Single custom hook                            |
| `__tests__/`       | Vitest + Testing Library tests                |

Shared UI → `src/common/components/`. Cross-module imports go through public
module surfaces (`routes.ts`, barrel `index.ts`) — never another module's internals.

---

## When to split

Split when a file has **more than one** of: React component, page, hook, schema,
service concern, or adapter.

---

## Tests

All tests live in `__tests__/` — never co-located beside source.

```
modules/home/
  __tests__/
    home.page.test.tsx
```

Target: ≥ 80% statement coverage on tested UI components. Tests use Testing Library
only in `__tests__/*.test.tsx`.

---

## Agent checklist (run on every module create/modify)

When creating or editing anything under `src/modules/` or `src/common/components/`:

1. **Match layout** use the canonical folder tree above.
2. **Split before merge** new page → `pages/`; new component → `components/`.
3. **Run checker** `npm run check:spaghetti` must pass.
4. **Run gates** `npm run typecheck` and `npm run test` for touched modules.
5. **Update docs** `docs/FRONTEND.mdc` if module structure changed.

If the checker fails, fix structure — do not disable or bypass the rule.
